    <statement><p>Find a vector <m>\mathbf{a}</m> that has the same direction as <m>\langle -10, 7, 10 \rangle</m> but has length <m>4</m>.</p>
<p>Answer: <m>\mathbf{a} =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left&lt;-2.5349,1.77443,2.5349\right&gt;</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>SOLUTION</p>
<p>The given vector has length <m>\left| \langle -10, 7, 10 \rangle \right|
= \sqrt{(-10)^2+7^2+10^2}= \sqrt{249}</m>, so a unit vector in the direction of 
<m>\langle -10, 7, 10 \rangle</m> is 
<m>\mathbf u = \frac{1}{\sqrt{249}}\langle -10, 7, 10 \rangle</m>.</p>
<p>A vector in the same direction but with length  <m>4</m>  is</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle 4 \mathbf u = \frac{4}{\sqrt{249}} \langle -10, 7, 10 \rangle 
=  \left \langle \frac{-40}{\sqrt{249}} , \frac{28}{\sqrt{249}},
\frac{40}{\sqrt{249}} \right \rangle</m>.</p>
</solution>
